          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341845",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is/are correct? (Mark all the appropriate choices)</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>In a distributive lattice, every element should have at most one complement.</li>\n\t<li>In a complemented lattice, every element should have at least one complement.</li>\n\t<li>In a boolean lattice, every element should have exactly one complement.</li>\n\t<li>In a boolean lattice, every element should have at least&nbsp;one complement.</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "A;B;C;D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,lattice,multiple-selects",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341799",
          "text": "<p>In the event of an emergency, the pilot was trained to $\\underline{\\text{jettison}}$ excess fuel from the aircraft.<br>\nThe underlined word is closest in meaning to:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>plummet</li>\n\t<li>whip</li>\n\t<li>abandon</li>\n\t<li>sleep</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,normal,verbal-aptitude,word-meaning",
          "category": "Verbal Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341831",
          "text": "<p>How many permutations of the letters ABCDEFGHIJKL contain the string ACDKL?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$7!$</li>\n\t<li>$\\frac{12!}{5!}$</li>\n\t<li>$8!$</li>\n\t<li>None of these</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,combinatory",
          "category": "Combinatory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341795",
          "text": "<p>In what ratio must milk $A$ at $Rs.\\,21.50$ per litre be mixed with milk $B$ at $Rs.\\,32.30$ per litre, so that the mixture be worth&nbsp;$Rs. 23$ per litre?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$93:15$</li>\n\t<li>$15:93$</li>\n\t<li>$3:5$</li>\n\t<li>$9:5$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,numerical-computation,quantitative-aptitude,mixtures",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341809",
          "text": "<p>Let $A=\\{a,b,c,d,e\\}$. The total number of unordered pairs of disjoint subsets of $A$ is equal to?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$3^{5}$</li>\n\t<li>$5^{3}$</li>\n\t<li>$102$</li>\n\t<li>$122$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,set-theory&algebra,set-theory",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341825",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is VALID?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$\\neg \\forall x\\exists y[(x\\leq y)\\rightarrow(x+y)&lt;0]\\Longleftrightarrow \\exists x\\forall y[(x&gt;y)\\wedge(x+y)\\leq 0]$</li>\n\t<li>$\\forall x\\exists y[(x\\leq y)\\rightarrow(x+y)&lt;0]\\Longleftrightarrow \\exists x\\forall y[(x&gt;y)\\vee(x+y)\\leq 0]$</li>\n\t<li>$\\neg \\forall x\\exists y[(x\\geq y)\\rightarrow(x+y)&gt;0]\\Longleftrightarrow \\exists x\\forall y[(x&gt;y)\\wedge(x+y)\\leq 0]$</li>\n\t<li>$\\neg \\exists x \\forall y[(x&lt;y)\\rightarrow\\forall z(x&lt;z&lt;y)]\\Longleftrightarrow \\forall x \\exists y &nbsp;\\exists z [(z\\leq x&lt;y)\\vee (x&lt;y\\leq&nbsp;z)]$&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,first-order-logic,mathematical-logic",
          "category": "Mathematical Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341803",
          "text": "<p>Let $f:R\\rightarrow R$ be defined by $f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{4+x^{2}},x\\in R.$<br>\nThen the range of $f$ is:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$\\:R-\\left[-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{4}\\right]$</li>\n\t<li>$\\:R-\\left[-2,2\\right]$</li>\n\t<li>$\\:(-2,2)-\\{0\\}$</li>\n\t<li>$\\:\\left[-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{4}\\right]$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,set-theory&algebra,functions",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341839",
          "text": "<p>The following propositional statement simplifies to<br>\n$\\ (\\neg P\\leftrightarrow \\neg Q)\\vee (\\neg P\\leftrightarrow Q)$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$P\\wedge Q$</li>\n\t<li>True</li>\n\t<li>$P\\rightarrow Q$</li>\n\t<li>False</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,propositional-logic,mathematical-logic",
          "category": "Mathematical Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341791",
          "text": "The number of generators for the cyclic group of order $2020$ is ________",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "800",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,numerical-answers,group-theory,set-theory&algebra,cyclic-group",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341849",
          "text": "<p>If the size (path length) of the longest chain in the following Hasse diagram is denoted by $a$ and that of the longest antichain is denoted by $b,$ then $a+b =$__________<br>\n<img alt=\"\" height=\"298\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"242\"></p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "5",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,numerical-answers,partial-order",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341833",
          "text": "<p>Read the following statements:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\">\n\t<li>If Raju spends two hours playing cricket, then he can not finish his Discrete Mathematics homework.</li>\n\t<li>If Raju finishes his Discrete Mathematics homework, then he will do well in his next test.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Based on the information above, which of the following is logically correct?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>If Raju does not finish his Discrete Mathematics homework, then he spent two hours playing cricket.</li>\n\t<li>If Raju finishes his Discrete Mathematics homework, then he did not spend two hours playing cricket.</li>\n\t<li>If Raju does well in his next test, then he did not spend two hours playing cricket.</li>\n\t<li>If Raju does not finish his Discrete Mathematics homework, then he does not do well in his next test.</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,propositional-logic",
          "category": "Mathematical Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341813",
          "text": "<p>Given the following two sets</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>$A=\\{1,a^{2}-2a+3\\}$</li>\n\t<li>$B=\\{a+2,a^{2}+2,a^{2}-3\\}$</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>If $A\\cap B=\\{6\\}, a$ is ________</p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "3",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,numerical-answers,set-theory&algebra,set-theory",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341811",
          "text": "<p>Let $X$ and $Y$ be two sets containing four and three elements respectively. Then the number of subsets of the set $X\\times Y,$ each having at least four elements?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$2048$</li>\n\t<li>$4096$</li>\n\t<li>$3797$</li>\n\t<li>$3410$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,combinatory",
          "category": "Combinatory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341805",
          "text": "If $f(x)=5x+2$ and $g(x)=3x-4$, what is the value of $a$ if $(f\\circ g^{-1}\\circ f^{-1})(a) = 4?$",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "-12",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,numerical-answers,set-theory&algebra,functions,function-inverse,function-composition",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341821",
          "text": "The total number of ways in which $4$ notes of different denominations can be put into the purses of $3$ persons so that no purse is empty is ________",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "36",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,numerical-answers,combinatory,balls-in-bins",
          "category": "Combinatory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341797",
          "text": "<p>Evaluate $i^{2023} + i^{2022} + i^{2021} + i^{2020}$, where $i = \\sqrt{-1}.$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$0$</li>\n\t<li>$2$</li>\n\t<li>$-2i$</li>\n\t<li>$2i$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,complex-number,quantitative-aptitude",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341823",
          "text": "<p>Let the universe be a school, and let $x$ and $y$ range over<br>\nthe students of a class. Define the predicate $P(x, y)$ as<br>\n$$P(x, y) :x\\ \\text{loves}\\ y.$$<br>\nMatch the following English sentences into Quantified predicates.<br>\n$$\\begin{array}{|cl|cc|}&nbsp;\\hline<br>\n&amp; \\textbf{English sentences} &amp; &amp; \\textbf{Quantified predicates}\\\\ \\hline&nbsp;<br>\n(i)&amp; \\text{All students love some student} &amp;(1) &amp; \\forall x\\forall y &nbsp;P(x,y)\\\\ \\hline&nbsp;<br>\n(ii)&amp; \\text{There are some students who love all of the other students}&amp;(2) &amp;\\exists x\\exists y &nbsp;P(x,y) \\\\ \\hline<br>\n(iii)&amp; \\text{All students love each other}&amp; (3)&amp;\\forall x\\exists y P(x,y) \\\\ \\hline&nbsp;<br>\n(iv)&amp;\\text{There are some students who love some of the other students} &amp; (4)&amp;\\exists x\\forall y &nbsp;P(x,y)\\\\ \\hline \\end{array}$$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>i-3, ii-4, iii-1, iv-2</li>\n\t<li>i-4, ii-3, iii-1, iv-2</li>\n\t<li>i-2, ii-1, iii-4, iv-3</li>\n\t<li>i-3, ii-3, iii-1, iv-2</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,first-order-logic,mathematical-logic",
          "category": "Mathematical Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341829",
          "text": "<p>What is the solution to the following recurrence relation?</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>$T(n) = 3T(n-1) + 1$</li>\n\t<li>$T(1) = 1$</li>\n</ul>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$3^{n}$</li>\n\t<li>$3^{n-1}$</li>\n\t<li>$3^{n}-1$</li>\n\t<li>$\\frac{3^{n}-1}{2}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,recurrence-relation,combinatory",
          "category": "Combinatory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341847",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following posets is not a boolean algebra, where $D_n$ is set of all divisors of integer $n$ and $(D_n, /)$ is partial order with division operator?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$(D_{10}, /)$</li>\n\t<li>$(D_{33}, /)$</li>\n\t<li>$(D_{30}, /)$</li>\n\t<li>$(D_{20}, /)$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,easy,boolean-algebra,partial-order",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341819",
          "text": "<p>The generating function corresponding to $4,5,7,10,14,19,25,\\dots $ is ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>$\\frac{4}{1-x} + \\frac{x}{(1-x)^3}$</li>\n\t<li>$\\frac{2}{1-x} + \\frac{x}{(1-x)^3}$</li>\n\t<li>$\\frac{4}{1-x} + \\frac{x}{(1-x)^2}$</li>\n\t<li>$\\frac{x}{(1-x)^3}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,generating-functions,combinatory",
          "category": "Combinatory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341815",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is/are correct? $(P(S)$ denotes the power set of $S)$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-roman\">\n\t<li>$P(\\phi) = \\{\\phi\\} $</li>\n\t<li>$P(P(\\phi)) = \\{\\phi,\\{\\phi\\}\\} $</li>\n\t<li>The power set of $\\{1,2,3,\\phi\\}$ contains $16$ elements</li>\n\t<li>All the subsets of the set $\\{\\phi,1,2\\}=\\{\\phi,\\{\\phi\\},\\{1\\},\\{2\\},\\{\\phi,1\\},\\{\\phi,2\\},\\{1,2\\},\\{\\phi,1,2\\}\\}$</li>\n\t<li>$P(P(P(\\phi)))=\\{\\phi,\\{\\phi\\},\\{\\{\\phi\\}\\}, \\{\\phi,\\{\\phi\\}\\}\\}$</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n\t<li>Only i, iii, v</li>\n\t<li>Only ii, iv, v</li>\n\t<li>Only i, ii, iii and iv</li>\n\t<li>All of these are correct</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-mix-1,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,power-set",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "341841",
          "text": "If $f(x) =3x-6$, what is the value of $f(f(f^{-1}(3)))?$",
